================================================================================
Modifications made to the original Codex source
================================================================================

As required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, this is a statement of the
changes made to the upstream files carried in this repository.

Files modified (8):

  codex/blueprints/app.py          Treat an all-digit search term as an explicit
                                   root id rather than free text. A MaleCNS
                                   synonym can contain another cell's id as a
                                   substring (e.g. "fru-M-100094" contains
                                   "10009"), which made the search ambiguous and
                                   bounced it to the results page.
  codex/data/brain_regions.py      Accept the MaleCNS side spelling "(L)"/"(R)"
                                   alongside FAFB's "_L"/"_R" when deriving a
                                   neuropil's side and base name, and merge the
                                   MaleCNS regions into the region tables.
  codex/data/local_data_loader.py  Read and write the data CSVs as UTF-8 with
                                   newline="" throughout. Python's default
                                   Windows codec is cp1252, which crashed on the
                                   MaleCNS labels.csv.gz.
  codex/data/neurotransmitters.py  Add histamine (HA) and UNK, which MaleCNS
                                   predicts and FlyWire 783 never emits.
  codex/data/versions.py           Register the "malecns" data version and name
                                   both versions by dataset rather than by
                                   snapshot number alone.
  codex/service/cell_details.py    Convert soma positions per dataset instead of
                                   assuming FlyWire voxels, and guard the
                                   neurotransmitter averages against transmitter
                                   types a given dataset does not carry.
  codex/utils/formatting.py        Add nanometre-to-voxel conversion for MaleCNS,
                                   which is 8 nm isotropic against FAFB's
                                   4/4/40 nm, and a dataset-dispatching wrapper.
  codex/utils/nglui.py             Point 3D links at the correct volume per
                                   dataset - FlyWire for FAFB, Janelia's
                                   neuroglancer for MaleCNS - and pass the soma
                                   position through so the view opens on the cell.

Files added (2):

  codex/data/malecns_regions.py    Generated MaleCNS neuropil region definitions
                                   (produced by lab/gen_malecns_regions.py).
  codex/data/malecns_roi_naming.py ROI renaming to resolve a collision: Codex
                                   uppercases region names, which collapses the
                                   mushroom-body alpha lobe (aL) onto the
                                   antennal lobe (AL). MB lobes are prefixed.

Directories added (entirely new work, not derived from Codex):

  lab/                             DuckDB build and query layer spanning both
                                   connectomes.
  sim/                             Embodied simulation: spiking brain, metabolism,
                                   arena, and the NeuroMechFly/MuJoCo body.

================================================================================
Third-party data and software
================================================================================

The connectome datasets are NOT distributed in this repository and are NOT
covered by its licence. They carry their own terms:

  FlyWire FAFB connectome, version 783
    https://flywire.ai  -  see the FlyWire citation guidelines before use.
    Dorkenwald et al. and Schlegel et al., Nature 2024.

  Janelia MaleCNS, version 1.0
    https://neuprint.janelia.org  -  CC-BY 4.0.
    HHMI Janelia Research Campus.

Third-party software used by sim/ but not redistributed here:

  NeuroMechFly / flygym                 https://github.com/NeLy-EPFL/flygym
    Neuroengineering Laboratory, EPFL. The biomechanical fly model, its
    ommatidial retina, and the MuJoCo scene composition API.
    Wang-Chen et al., Nature Methods 2024.

  MuJoCo                                https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco
    Google DeepMind. Apache-2.0.

The leaky integrate-and-fire parameterisation used in sim/brain.py follows:

  Shiu, Sterne, Spiller et al., "A leaky integrate-and-fire computational model
  based on the connectome of the entire adult Drosophila brain reveals insights
  into sensorimotor processing", Nature 2024.
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07763-9
